---
layout: layouts/base.njk
---
{#-
  Information-page layout (SPEC §7.4; HANDOFF §6.5; boards Info-*.dc.html):
  teal title band, then the content in one column. There is no side menu
  (SPEC §7.5, §22): the header and footer link to every information page.
  Pages in content/pages/ use it by default (pages.11tydata.js), which also
  sets page_id to the file name and the URL to /<file name>/.

  Front-matter contract:
    title     required. <title>, and the H1 unless `heading` is set
    summary   required. Lede under the H1, and the meta description
              (and the search summary in M2)
    eyebrow   optional. Label above the H1. Default "Information";
              set it to "" for none
    heading   optional. H1 text when it differs from the title
    band      optional. "standard" (default) or "hero" (About: lede beside
              the H1, settling arc at the base)
    styles    optional. Extra stylesheets under src/css/, e.g.
              ["pages/help.css"] -> /css/pages/help.css
    search    optional. false keeps the page out of the search index (M2)

  The content column has the classes `info-body info-body--<page_id>`, so a
  page's stylesheet can target it (e.g. `.info-body--help`). The column is a
  flex column with a section gap; each top-level child is one section. It is
  as wide as the container, so card grids and tables can use the width,
  while headings, paragraphs and plain lists keep the reading measure, and a
  panel of text ends with its text (site.css §9).

  Example (content/pages/help.md):
    ---
    title: Get more help
    summary: This program can help with many sleep problems, but not all. Here is when to talk to someone, and who.
    styles: ["pages/help.css"]
    ---
-#}
<main id="main" class="info-page{% if band == 'hero' %} info-page--hero{% endif %}">
  {% include "partials/title-band.njk" %}
  <div class="info-layout container">
    <div class="info-body info-body--{{ page_id }}">
      {{ content | safe }}
    </div>
  </div>
</main>
